{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444601-w20-how-to-assert-oneself-as-a-comparatively-weak-character-in-a-sept","id":1444601,"title":"W20: How to assert oneself as a comparatively \"weak\" character in a sept?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-18T23:33:13-07:00","id":1444601,"title":"W20: How to assert oneself as a comparatively \"weak\" character in a sept?","content":"Hello everybody,<br /> <br /> I come to you again asking for a bit of advice.<br /> <br /> My playgroup plays WTA now for approximately half a year. More or less one session per week (exceptions happen of course due to personal matters).<br /> <br /> I play my second character now after my first one died due to very unfortunate circumstances and bad rolls. Shit happens, lets move on.<br /> <br /> Now I play the packs theurge, and one of only three Theurges left in the Sept after an attempt for a coup. One of whom is an Elder, the other one Keeper of the Land.<br /> <br /> The one thing that I noticed during our half year-playtime is that the &quot;fighters&quot; always seem to reign surpreme or have more leeway in many situations. As much in combat as in social situation. For the later they just threaten to challenge your character to combat if they dont get their way or do the &quot;stare down&quot;. Garou Society can be very martial and without compromise, as I understand it. I absolutely accept that from a player perspective.<br /> <br /> Since my character is not exactly a great combatant (for a Garou), he had to back out of many arguments. As a Metis he cant expect to reliably be tendet to afterwards if &quot;mistakes&quot; happen. Fortunetly those conflicts never happened in the pack, they are all super dandy with each other, but with other sept members of the same societal Rank or one above.<br /> <br /> So I come from a VTM-focused Background where my characters always had an easier time to outmaneuver potential rivals through non-combative means. In our WTA Game I can't think of many other means to be honest. Probably because I am not that knowlegable about WTA as I am about VTM. I considered leveraging his position as one of the few Theurges in the Sept. Asking Spirits for help with other sept-members seems petty to him from an in-character perspective. And too dangerous. He had a very bad experience with an air elemental that summoned a Typhoon, which heavily backfired and almost killed the pack.<br /> <br /> I considered for him to ask for other challenges than combat. As I understand it challenges must be appropriate for the capabilities of challenger and challenged.<br /> <br /> Of course I reflected on if my character was unintentionally looking for trouble. Keeping your head low as a Metis always seems to be a good option but arguments happen with a fuse as short as that of many Garou. My characters included.<br /> <br /> So long story short. Do you have some advice for me to better portray my character in these situations? Reading advice for sourcebooks is also very welcome, though I try to limit myself to W20 books. Since the situation is strictly in-character I did not want to talk with my ST about this yet.<br /> <br /> I hope this topic is not discussed to death on these forums. During my internet seach I only found threads from STs asking how to &quot;handle&quot; &quot;overpowered&quot; player characters which does not fit for this situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T00:57:57-07:00","id":1444607,"title":"","content":"Garou have a martial culture, and combat skills and physical prowess are always going to be prized. In most tribes (though not all), the higher rage auspices will tend to be the leaders. But there's always an important role played by other character types because the Garou aren't just fighters. They need people to contribute at all levels of society. Spiritualism, art, law, history, etc. are all vital.<br /> <br /> I don't know all the situations you are facing so it is hard to comment. If it is stuff that affects combat, fighting, defense, etc., then I'm not surprised the challenges are oriented towards physical combat. But a good Master of Challenge should be able to identify the nature of the dispute and determine a relevant challenge. And there should be a lot of disputes where it is more important to win a riddle contest, recite old lore, create a new epic poem, craft a useful fetish, or something else that should play to the strength of your character and others who have other skills than combat.<br /> <br /> It's also important to know who is doing the challenging. Typically the person being challenged determines the nature of the challenge. So it should never be the case of a bully going to up characters and taking away their stuff because he knows in advance he'll win any dispute.<br /> <br /> In terms of packs and septs, there should be ways known in advance of how to settle certain disputes, heavily based on pack and sept culture, which in turn should be based heavily on pack and caern totems, pack quests, and other culture. A pack under a totem of war will likely decide pack leadership challenges and other disputes in a martial fashion. But a pack under Unicorn or Chimera or Stag should have very different challenges to settle those same questions, because the totem (and likely the pack quest) makes other demands. Sept culture is likely heavily based on the caern totem and the type of caern. A caern of sacrifice with a caern totem of Fenris will likely require a lot of bloodshed, physical pain, combat, and the like. A caern of Gnosis with a caern totem of Owl would be very different. They would employ different approaches to the exact same challenges.<br /> <br /> The issue is whether the challenge is appropriate to the issue being decided. If it's not, the setting probably isn't being properly presented.<br /> <br /> So is the ST showing this? Or is the ST showing a much more constrained, and perhaps cookie cutter approach, to these issues? If you think the ST isn't giving enough thought to these other aspects of Garou culture or avenues of advancement, speak to the ST. And maybe your PC will speak about these things at the next sept moot. Talk with NPCs who are in a similar position than you - Theurges, Ragabash, and the less martially inclined members of the other auspices. Build a political coalition to make changes in the sept, if the ST will allow that.<br /> <br /> Another thing is to look at the Renown chart to see what it is that Garou value. There are lots of other things that earn Renown than just combat. Does the ST look at that as being equally valid? Is your character contributing to the sept in ways that generate Renown? Vampire is very individually based - what is in it for me? Werewolf is much more community based - how are you helping the society you are in?<br /> <br /> Another issue is the concept of chiminage. By doing favors for others, you accrue debt just like boons in vampire. You just need to be able to perform something other people need so they will approach you for it. Once you are useful, NPCs should be less likely wanting to anger you because you can cut off the supply of goodies.<br /> <br /> I do not know the specifics of your situation, but if I was a Theurge belonging to a sept and wanted to get recognition within it, become a leader by gaining followers, and becoming a respected voice in the sept, here are some things I might do:<br /> <br /> 1) Crafts Talens for the benefit of the sept leadership. The Sept Elders likely need talens like Bane Arrows, Gaia's Breath, Nightshade, Wyrm Scales, and others on an ongoing basis in order to protect the sept and fulfill sept needs.<br /> 2) Likewise other packs might need them as well, which can be exchanged in terms of chiminage. This might include use of other mystic rites or rites in general, like the rite of talisman dedication. There are lots of useful services a Theurge should be able to provide.<br /> 3) Make friends with spirits. You should have Spirit Speech and lots of other useful Gifts and rites. Treat spirits like real NPCs. Get to know the names they are known by, find out what things they need done, what they like and don't like. You can build Spirit Networks. You can gain favor of spirits. And you can tell spirits who are the Garou they should like or not like based on their reputation. If you have a good reputation with spirits, they should want to be nice to you and do you favors for any help you provided them. And the people you don't like will become the people they don't like. That will impact other Garou's ability to learn Gifts, create Talens or Fetishes, or get help in the Umbra.<br /> 4) Become a subject matter expert. Learn the lore of the setting, whether that be actual history of the setting, or simply a lot of things that often gets handwaved in game but represents real knowledge NPCs respect and want. Once you are recognized as that expert, people have to go to you if they want to use that. They need to offer chiminage in exchange, even if that ends up only being respect, tokens of gratitude, and the like.<br /> 5) Look for opportunities to resolve conflicts through non-violence. There are advantages of doing so for preserving the Veil, protecting kinfolk, learning lore that can help you defeat certain Wyrm creatures. That builds the case of resolving internal Garou disputes through non-violent means like riddle contests, storytelling, and other means of problem solving.<br /> 6) Look for things the sept needs, but doesn't have whether that be knowledge of certain rites, locations of Wyrm minions, protection of the local kinfolk community, or whatever.<br /> <br /> A lot of these things depend on a good ST. But even if your ST isn't currently thinking of these things, the ST can still be open to changing things once he understands how they can add to the game.<br /> <br /> In short, find allies, build coalitions, make yourself useful, and leverage your strengths. A metis theurge might never become sept leader, but can still gain a lot of informal authority or even formal leadership in the sept.<br /> <br /> Just keep in mind some of your problems might because the ST is purposefully doing things to undermine you because the NPCs would do that to a metis.<br /> <br /> I would start with having an OOC conversation with the ST and let her know that you are looking for ways for your Theurge to have more impact and gain followers in the sept, and you wanted to share some ideas. See what she says. Then build on that OOC conversation until you know how to proceed IC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T01:32:16-07:00","id":1444610,"title":"","content":"To expand on the above with something from the books:<br /> <br /> There are <b>three</b> primary types of challenges in Garou society; combat, facedowns, and gamecraft. Those that challenge Ragabash and Theurges best be ready for a challenge of wits and cunning over force because gamecraft heavily favors mental focused characters (and the Enigmas Knowledge for a traditional riddle-contest, but maybe other things if as Black Fox noted the game is less traditional).<br /> <br /> With it being traditional for the challenged to set the terms instead of the challenger, that alone level the playing field a lot. A lot of Septs and Tribes favor gamecraft challenges because it's the only one that doesn't risk violence (facedowns can result in Frenzies since Rage might be rolled instead of normal skills), and even if fairly hardcore strength focused groups it shouldn't lose face to have a gamecraft challenge over an intellectual dispute as a bare minimum. In a direct challenge, as opposed to a challenge petitioned to the Sept via the Master of the Challenge, Garou don't, at all, feel the challenged needs to be nice to the challenger; esp. if the challenge is bullying or petty. Ahrouns trying to force combat challenges are just brutes, not warriors, and need to prove the strength of their minds after all.<br /> <br /> The other thing to remember is that you don't need to challenge to get your way. Politics are part of Garou life, and getting the higher Ranked Garou of the Sept on your side is a much more potent tool. A lot of this if covered above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T02:04:25-07:00","id":1444611,"title":"","content":"Black Fox to the rescue! Thank you for the input as always <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some Information about the Sept and Caern:<br /> <br /> The Sept is one created by the ST located in rural Poland at a Caern of Healing. Sadly I do not know how to translate the Sept Totems Name into English. &quot;Menhir&quot; or &quot;Standing Stone&quot; might be appropriate. It is not one one of the major Tribe Totems.<br /> <br /> The Sept is lead by a triumvirate of Elders consisting of Red Talon Ahroun, Lupus Black Furie Philodox and Homid Silverfang Ahroun. On this I hav to correct myself. I misremembered the Furie as a Theurge. Which reduces the Number of Theurges in the Sept to only 2. My character an the Keeper of the Land, who is a Rank 3 Child of Gaia. They Silverfang Elder was the former &quot;Master of Challenge&quot;. After the coup he rose to Status of Elder. He is a very &quot;firm but fair&quot;-character and abhores bloodshed or severe injurie during challenge. His former position as of now seems to be vacant. The last moot did not appoint a new one. As of now the Sept is in a State of War with a construction company, with ties to subsidiary pentex owned companies, trying to encroach in on the territory.<br /> <br /> While reading your text I had a small epiphany. First of it seems I understood chiminage wrong. Always thought that was only for dealing and bartering with spirits. I really like your suggestions of making the character useful by creating Talens, making friends with Spirits (which was the reason for creating a theurge in the first place) and so on.<br /> <br /> The realisation I had is that we almost never have any Downtime now. It's always from &quot;plot&quot; to &quot;plot&quot;. Simple everyday play with the Sept was very nice in the beginning but became less and less with ongoing time. I am very much into roleplaying every bit out. My fellow players and friends not so much.<br /> <br /> My ST uses &quot;Rule Zero&quot; very much but more or less to move things along. For example when my Char is doing certain rites. Especially the Rite of Summoning. I asked him last time to let me roleplay the ritual out. He agreed to that. We'll have to see about that foru future sessions.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I think I know more WTA Lore than my ST but it is his &quot;chronicle&quot; so I don't want to be the &quot;Uhm actually&quot;-guy and undermine his position when he makes ingame statements. Please don't think of me as the &quot;humble brag&quot;-type. I am just glad to be a player after years of being a Vampire-ST (which I enjoy greatly dont get me wrong but its cool to be a player).<br /> <br /> Furthermore my fellow players seem to be very content with our Chronicle at the end of every game session and love their chars. So who am I to infringe on that? They are playing a Homid Bone Gnawer Ragabash and a Lupus Fianna Galliard. Both very much combat oriented in their playstyle. My friend who plays the Bone Gnawer is someone who needs a great deal of time to warm-up to his characters to confidently roleplay them. I am glad he got the hang of it now.<br /> <br /> My last criticism to my ST was the lack of consequenz for our characters temper. We lack horror moments almost entierly. We newer got in trouble for the ugly parts of being Garou like potentially losing your temper in the presence of Kinfolk or innocents.<br /> <br /> See I don't want to be the guy to shift all responsibility to the ST as I think that is unfair to him. He is very motivated when presenting us with new threats and enemies and does a great job in setting up the menace. He adores the Book of The Wyrm but I think he looks into the enemy section more than into Garou Matters themselves.<br /> <br /> The more I write the more I notice I'm derailing my own thread. Sorry about that. I am starting to think the original thread topic is not the problem but a &quot;symptom&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T02:15:24-07:00","id":1444613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444601-w20-how-to-assert-oneself-as-a-comparatively-weak-character-in-a-sept?p=1444610#post1444610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To expand on the above with something from the books:<br /> <br /> There are <b>three</b> primary types of challenges in Garou society; combat, facedowns, and gamecraft. Those that challenge Ragabash and Theurges best be ready for a challenge of wits and cunning over force because gamecraft heavily favors mental focused characters (and the Enigmas Knowledge for a traditional riddle-contest, but maybe other things if as Black Fox noted the game is less traditional).<br /> <br /> With it being traditional for the challenged to set the terms instead of the challenger, that alone level the playing field a lot. A lot of Septs and Tribes favor gamecraft challenges because it's the only one that doesn't risk violence (facedowns can result in Frenzies since Rage might be rolled instead of normal skills), and even if fairly hardcore strength focused groups it shouldn't lose face to have a gamecraft challenge over an intellectual dispute as a bare minimum. In a direct challenge, as opposed to a challenge petitioned to the Sept via the Master of the Challenge, Garou don't, at all, feel the challenged needs to be nice to the challenger; esp. if the challenge is bullying or petty. Ahrouns trying to force combat challenges are just brutes, not warriors, and need to prove the strength of their minds after all.<br /> <br /> The other thing to remember is that you don't need to challenge to get your way. Politics are part of Garou life, and getting the higher Ranked Garou of the Sept on your side is a much more potent tool. A lot of this if covered above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank your for expaning further <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That is very interesting.<br /> <br /> I would be glat to play the politics angle but as I understood it until now you can have Allies as much as you want but during a challenge you stand alone and have to win on your own accord.<br /> <br /> But I am going to keep in my that my character can always try spin the challenge in his favor or at least make it fair.<br /> <br /> In our games things get physical very very fast. Which is why my character keeps a low profile as I described. A Punch in the face is often deliviered very fast among the Cliaths of different packs. And from there the situation goes to shit because somebody &quot;botches&quot; the frenzy check.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T03:04:23-07:00","id":1444620,"title":"","content":"Throwing punches between packs at the drop of the hat is... kinda extreme even by Garou standards. Even more so if the Sept is at a Caern of Healing. While some tussling, snarling, and shoving around is to be expected, if it's regularly getting to the point of Frenzies (remember that Frenzies are a Renown loss, which many Cliath's can't afford) means the higher Ranked Garou aren't doing their jobs of keeping the youngsters in line.<br /> <br /> And while you are correct that during the challenge both parties stand alone, having friends in high places can help in a few ways:<br /> <br /> 1) Stepping in and setting the terms of the challenge (esp. Philodox and the Master of the Challenge) if the nature of the challenge would render it &quot;unjust,&quot; which sufficiently high Ranked Garou are within their rights to do and give characters they like an edge.<br /> <br /> 2) Picking a winner anyway. If an Elder walks up to some bickering Cliaths and demands to know what they're squabbling about, the Cliaths better answer, and the Elder can order one side to concede to the other; anyone on the losing side has to now challenge an Elder to get their way. An Elder tried of violence breaking out between packs because the Cliaths are too on edge can add on all sorts of things, like demanding the losing party perform the Rite of Contrition within a month or face punishments for disobeying orders. Etc. One of the reasons a lot of Garou don't like the Silver Fangs, is that they're extremely talented at using this for a sort of nepotism to control power.<br /> <br /> 3) Less extreme, the higher Ranks can still step in after the lower Ranks settle things, and for them to focus on cleaning up the messes they made to discourage this sort of conflict. Packs that don't keep their more hot tempered members in check get stuck with all the crappy jobs around the Sept, leaving the good jobs (esp. the Renown earning jobs) to packs that make sure to impress the Sept office holders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T04:30:41-07:00","id":1444625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444601-w20-how-to-assert-oneself-as-a-comparatively-weak-character-in-a-sept?p=1444620#post1444620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throwing punches between packs at the drop of the hat is... kinda extreme even by Garou standards. Even more so if the Sept is at a Caern of Healing. While some tussling, snarling, and shoving around is to be expected, if it's regularly getting to the point of Frenzies (remember that Frenzies are a Renown loss, which many Cliath's can't afford) means the higher Ranked Garou aren't doing their jobs of keeping the youngsters in line.<br /> <br /> And while you are correct that during the challenge both parties stand alone, having friends in high places can help in a few ways:<br /> <br /> 1) Stepping in and setting the terms of the challenge (esp. Philodox and the Master of the Challenge) if the nature of the challenge would render it &quot;unjust,&quot; which sufficiently high Ranked Garou are within their rights to do and give characters they like an edge.<br /> <br /> 2) Picking a winner anyway. If an Elder walks up to some bickering Cliaths and demands to know what they're squabbling about, the Cliaths better answer, and the Elder can order one side to concede to the other; anyone on the losing side has to now challenge an Elder to get their way. An Elder tried of violence breaking out between packs because the Cliaths are too on edge can add on all sorts of things, like demanding the losing party perform the Rite of Contrition within a month or face punishments for disobeying orders. Etc. One of the reasons a lot of Garou don't like the Silver Fangs, is that they're extremely talented at using this for a sort of nepotism to control power.<br /> <br /> 3) Less extreme, the higher Ranks can still step in after the lower Ranks settle things, and for them to focus on cleaning up the messes they made to discourage this sort of conflict. Packs that don't keep their more hot tempered members in check get stuck with all the crappy jobs around the Sept, leaving the good jobs (esp. the Renown earning jobs) to packs that make sure to impress the Sept office holders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see I see.<br /> <br /> It is indeed very common for npc characters to frenzy often in our chronicle. Insults, losing the Staredown and the aforementioned throwing of punches. As I said frenzy did not have any severe consequenzes in our chronicle yet apart from some minor renown loss for some npcs which does not seem to affect their standing.<br /> <br /> The coup I mentioned robbed the Sept oft many Garou of middling Rank. We have the three Elders. 5 Members of Rank 3-4 and a bunch Ranks 1 and 2.<br /> <br /> The Elders and higher ups are very hands off at the moment because they do all the &quot;strategic work&quot; back at the sept for the conflict with the construction company, which leaves many packs of Rank 1s and 2s to do the &quot;Dirty Work&quot;. Who of course think they know best how to handle the operations. In the approach we are given a relativly free hand story-wise which makes the conflicts more frequent because the Elders give vague orders.<br /> <br /> All your suggestions are really great and I wish it were like that, but at the moment I am not sure how to convey all of that to my ST without coming of as just reading him a very long list of how I want him to change his playstyle to accomadate me. I know this statement is rather hyperbolic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T06:56:45-07:00","id":1444646,"title":"","content":"Why would you have to change his running style? Just have your character react to any challenge with gamecraft.<br /> <br /> Besides, depending on the tribe of your character, being a metis means they might be safer in the sidelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T08:19:05-07:00","id":1444664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444601-w20-how-to-assert-oneself-as-a-comparatively-weak-character-in-a-sept?p=1444646#post1444646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you have to change his running style? Just have your character react to any challenge with gamecraft.<br /> <br /> Besides, depending on the tribe of your character, being a metis means they might be safer in the sidelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right I should do that. To be honest I think I got a bit carried away at the and and did go on an unnessecary tangent.<br /> <br /> Again thank you for all the suggestions again. I'll try practising it for our next session <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T10:33:48-07:00","id":1444677,"title":"","content":"Remember that there's nothing wrong with expressing your desires to the ST about how to make the game more fun for you. Be polite of course, and try to offer up ways to avoid making things unfun for the ST or other players, but in the end they can't do their part in helping you enjoy gaming together if you don't speak to them about it.<br /> <br /> You could, for example, ask about developing one of the Athro or Elder level NPCs as an Ally, but express that you want them more active with the lower Ranking packs if your going to work towards having Background dots invested in the NPC; and make sneak in a point about Rank giving bonuses to resist Frenzies to your Ally isn't making things worse by showing up.<br /> <br /> We can help you find support for things in the books if it would help further, but we can't do that much about things that come down to group dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T10:38:56-07:00","id":1444858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444601-w20-how-to-assert-oneself-as-a-comparatively-weak-character-in-a-sept?p=1444677#post1444677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could, for example, ask about developing one of the Athro or Elder level NPCs as an Ally, but express that you want them more active with the lower Ranking packs if your going to work towards having Background dots invested in the NPC; and make sneak in a point about Rank giving bonuses to resist Frenzies to your Ally isn't making things worse by showing up.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this kind of approach.<br /> <br /> Thank you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}